        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ken Burns; Charles McDowell, Jr.; Mark Twain; Samuel Clemens; Sam R. Watkins\n- Works: Baseball; Tunisian Victory; The Congress; The Civil War; Mark Twain\n- Topics: Baseball; North Africa Campaign\n\nFacts:\n- Tunisian Victory is a 1944 Anglo-American propaganda film about victories in the North Africa Campaign.\n- Baseball is a 1994 American television documentary miniseries created by Ken Burns about the game of baseball.\n- Charles McDowell, Jr. appeared in an interview in Ken Burns' documentary The Congress.\n- Charles McDowell, Jr. provided the character voice for Sam R. Watkins in Ken Burns' documentary The Civil War.\n- Charles McDowell, Jr. provided a character voice and consultation for Ken Burns' documentary Baseball.\n- Ken Burns produced the documentary film Mark Twain in 2001.\n- Mark Twain is also known as Samuel Clemens.\n- Mark Twain aired on the Public Broadcasting System on January 14 and 15, 2002.",
